# Line-ending policy.
#
# `tests/test_launchers.py` regenerates the .cmd launchers and asserts they are
# byte-identical to the committed ones.  With core.autocrlf=true a clone would
# rewrite their line endings and that test would fail on the very first run, so
# every checkout has to reproduce exactly the bytes that were committed.
* -text

# These are text; keep them LF everywhere so generated == committed.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.pyw   text eol=lf
*.cmd   text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# Never let Git touch these.
vendor/ffmpeg/* binary
assets/*        binary
*.png           binary
*.ico           binary
*.flac          binary
*.mflac         binary
*.qmcflac       binary
